<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Interfaz 1.4 (ADR-055 amendment): the Welcome view. It hosts the
  first-run / update wizard as an inline stepper (Observatory -> Targets
  -> Data) instead of the old modal QWizard, wrapped in a painted night
  sky.

  The structure, texts and tooltips live here (ADR-005). gui/widgets/
  welcome_setup.py wires the signals, swaps skyHero for the real painted
  hero (WelcomeSky), fills the "your night, now" strip, the kind cards and
  the migration report, and gates navigation on the update's Data step.

  The whole page is compact on purpose: it has to fit the content area of
  a 1280x860 window (~770 px) WITHOUT squeezing the forms, which is what
  made the old layout collapse. The two lists that can grow without bound
  (the kind cards, the migration report) keep their own scroll box with a
  capped height; the host wraps the page in one outer scroll as a safety
  net for short screens (gui/widgets/welcome_setup.py).

  Two slots are placeholders for custom widgets and MUST stay QWidget:
  skyHero (the painted sky) and card1Chips (the coloured kind chips).
-->
